# =============================================================================
# WILDCARDS -- KEEP THIS BLOCK LAST
# =============================================================================
# Cloudflare matches static rules on a fast path and evaluates splat/placeholder rules in order, so every static rule above must precede these. With a wildcard sitting mid-file, Wrangler warns on all 71 static rules below it on every deploy, which buries real warnings.
#
# Verified safe to demote: no static rule above is matched by any of these, so none was ever shadowed and none changes behavior by moving up.
#
# Order within this block matters. The two :slug rules must stay after the splats and after every explicit legacy rule (e.g. /work/photography/), or they swallow them.

# Old WordPress project archives -> work index
/project-type/*                   /work                             301
/project-attributes/*             /work                             301

# Blog catch-all. Destination is the /journal INDEX, never /journal/:splat -- journal slugs do NOT match old blog slugs, so :splat manufactured redirects to non-existent pages (a 301 -> 404, worse than a 404). Catches what the specific /blog rules miss: .html forms, WordPress tag/category/date archives, any unmapped slug.
/blog/*                           /journal                          301

# Trailing slash -> bare, for case studies and journal posts
/work/:slug/                      /work/:slug                       301
/journal/:slug/                   /journal/:slug                    301
